# Step 1-2: Find the minimum and maximum elements of each array
# Step 3: Initialize an index variable to 0. This index variable will be used in step 4.
# Step 4: Compare the first element of the second array (arr2_min) with the last element of the first array (arr1_max).
# If they are equal, 4 and 7 are common elements.
# Step 5: Recursively sort the sub-arrays containing elements after the first element of each array.
# The first element of the sorted sub-arrays will be potential common elements.
# Step 6: Starting from the next higher element of the second array (arr2_max), compare it with arr1_max.
# If they are equal, 4 and 7 are common elements.
# Step 7: Recursively sort the sub-arrays containing elements after the arr1_max in the first array, and arr2_max in the second array.
# The first element of the sorted sub-arrays will be potential common elements.
# Step 8: Repeat step 6 until no element is left to be compared.
# If two sub-array are already sorted, there's no need to further compare their elements.

# In this example, the common elements are 4 and 7.
